{
  "_comment": [
    "Example MCP server registration for Claude Code.",
    "",
    "Copy this file to one of:",
    "  - $EMBERVY_HOME/.mcp.json                (project-scoped)",
    "  - ~/.claude/settings.json under \"mcpServers\" (user-scoped)",
    "",
    "Then start Claude Code with:",
    "  claude --dangerously-load-development-channels server:app",
    "",
    "or simply run start-claude-loop.sh, which sets the same flag.",
    "",
    "The 'app' name must match EMBERVY_CHANNELS in your .env (default 'app').",
    "",
    "The installer also registers the memory worker as 'lore' (type http,",
    "url <EMBERVY_URL>/mcp, Authorization: Bearer <EMBERVY_API_KEY>) — the agent",
    "sees its tools as mcp__lore__wake, mcp__lore__find, … (the Lore, its",
    "working memory; houses from before called the server 'memory').",
    "",
    "The script path is absolute on purpose: Claude Code ignores \"cwd\" and",
    "would look for mcp.ts in the house folder, where it does not exist."
  ],
  "mcpServers": {
    "app": {
      "command": "bun",
      "args": ["run", "/opt/embervy/Claude/app/mcp.ts"],
      "cwd": "/opt/embervy/Claude/app",
      "env": {
        "EMBERVY_HOME": "/opt/embervy",
        "EMBERVY_APP_HOST": "127.0.0.1",
        "EMBERVY_APP_PORT": "3030",
        "USER_LABEL": "User",
        "AGENT_LABEL": "Agent"
      }
    }
  }
}
